WEBVTT

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.670
I see.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.090
Thanks for your time.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.530
<i>Not enough information...</i>

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.870
<i>Will we have to use the Horologium as bait?</i>

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.770
There's that phantom thief!

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:26.880
Get him!

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.690
Vampire Requiem

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.180
Looks like they're the best of friends now.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.860
And he still doesn't like me at all...

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:18.160
Sisi, I guess you're a boy after all, huh?

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.180
I was kidding! It was just 
a joke! Don't get mad!

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.760
Um... Van?

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.450
If you're looking for Lupin, 
he left earlier

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.340
and hasn't come back yet.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.290
Have a seat. There's enough 
breakfast for you, too.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.630
Your cooking isn't to my taste.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.300
Huh?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.220
You've never even eaten it!

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.720
Good morning, Van.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:52.220
Hey!

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.610
Come to think of it, there's an 
interesting new article out.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.840
"Phantom thief under the moon appears"...

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.730
"Flying in the sky and 
disappearing like a fog"?

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.940
That guy showed up again, huh?

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.880
Yes, and it appears he used the same methods 
as in the previous serial thefts.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.750
They say all the stolen items have 
been vampire family treasures.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.530
Vampires?

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:29.770
They're a type of demi-human with remarkable
 physical abilities and very long lifespans.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.270
They have always inspired 
a sense of awe in humans.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.610
Awe...

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.770
I'd wager you must be 
quite familiar with them,

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:40.310
"Hero" Van Helsing?

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.550
It's said that vampire treasures 
are always very valuable items.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.670
It's no surprise that they 
would be targets of theft.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:51.680
They've had the Yard on high alert. 
Wonder how he got away with it.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:54.780
He might even put Lupin—whose whole
gimmick is his audacity—to shame.

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:57.310
What was that about me?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.140
Welcome back.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.640
The antisocial four-eyes 
is waiting for you.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.210
Oh? I see.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.230
I see everyone's here. Perfect timing.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.680
I just heard some good news.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.930
Steal Finis and the train he's riding in?!

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:16.870
Yeah.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.470
I found out he'll be boarding 
a train to London in two weeks

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.950
to inspect a war plant on the north side.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:29.460
The plan is to strike there and abduct 
Finis, the leader of Twilight.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.060
This doesn't mean I'm on 
board with Impey's idea,

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.520
but doesn't this seem like the 
fastest way to get information,

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:39.110
both on Twilight's terrorist 
plot and on Isaac?

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.780
Sounds good! I'm in!

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.400
The idea of stealing the 
whole train surprised me,

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.550
but it looks like our chance 
wasted no time presenting itself.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:50.710
How did you get that information?

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.720
This is an intelligence agency 
we're talking about.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:58.720
I'm the gentleman thief, Arsène Lupin.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:02.170
There's nothing I can't steal.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.660
Whether it's a jewel, a person,

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.960
or classified information.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:15.050
During his inspection, security will be 
weakest when he's on the train.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:18.770
If you'll all help me, we can pull it off.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.370
Sure, but Cardia, you'll have to stay here.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.250
Huh?

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:25.660
You're what Twilight wants, after all.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.240
Just let us handle—

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.730
No. We'll bring her.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.620
She's the monster that Twilight is after.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.730
She can be our trump card 
if it comes to it.

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:38.370
You're still talking like that?

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:42.040
My only objective is to take out Finis.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.280
If you want my help, 
you'll accept my terms.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.650
You—

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:48.950
That's...

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.830
I hesitate to agree to that,

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.280
but Van's strength is crucial to this plan.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.740
I'll go with you.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.780
If you're all going, I'll go with you.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.040
Because...

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.050
I'm one of you.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.460
But Cardia, see...

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.810
All right. You can help me, too.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.540
Whoa, Lupin! What are you saying?

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.570
Of course, I have no intention 
of giving Cardia to Twilight.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:20.130
You'll learn to protect yourself.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:22.920
Starting today, we'll be training you.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.100
Training?

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:27.570
All of us here have different abilities.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:30.280
We have England's leading alchemist,

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.310
a well-informed noble,

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.530
a battle-hardened hero,

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.430
an engineer who's a whiz with 
machines, if nothing else...

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.320
Hey!

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.420
And a great thief with a 100% success rate.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:45.170
The perfect set of instructors to teach 
you how to defend yourself, right?

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.710
He's right.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:49.780
We'll do whatever we can to help you.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.720
This all sounds like great fun.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.970
I'm worried...

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.530
I'll work hard,

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:00.840
so will you be my teacher too, Impey?

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:03.060
T-T-T-Teacher?!

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.620
That has such an attractive ring to it!

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:11.620
Okay! Teacher Impey is gonna whip up 
his best invention ever for you!

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:14.280
If you give her something, 
make sure it's safe.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.670
If it ends up exploding, 
there'll be hell to pay.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.740
In that case, maybe we should teach 
her how to treat wounds first.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.630
Hey, come on, you two!

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.200
Have a little faith in 
this genius engineer!

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.870
Impey, that's bad manners.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:27.580
Foolishness.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.910
You seem really... I don't know... alive.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.800
Like you're having a lot of fun.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:00.210
Is it... fun?

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:03.610
There's so much to remember. I'm very busy.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.450
That's a good thing.

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:09.510
Keeping busy with work is 
better for a person's health.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:12.860
Fran seems busy all the time,

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.870
but sometimes his face is very pale.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.420
That's from overwork.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:19.780
We've got all the information,

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.670
and the inventions we'll need 
for the plan are coming along.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.230
We're in great shape.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.950
Cardia's training is going well, too.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.680
She's already learned how to drive!

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:33.940
She knows a great deal about the geography 
and history of London now, too.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:36.020
It's thanks to all of you.

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:40.210
Well, the most important thing will 
probably be martial arts, though.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:45.960
Did you call me here to listen to all this?

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.630
No. I have a proposal.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.460
This is the "phantom thief under 
the moon" who keeps going

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.220
after vampire family treasures.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.710
Reward money is being offered for him now.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:09:00.480
Word has it he'll be targeting the 
Adele and Brutus Firm's auction next.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:04.510
Cardia, as the finishing 
touch to your training,

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.480
I think we should capture him.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.760
Finishing touch?

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.970
Better than jumping straight 
to fighting Twilight, right?

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:14.310
We're starting to run out of funds, anyway.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:16.940
Huh? How much do we have?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:21.600
At this rate, it won't be long before 
we can't even feed ourselves.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.490
What?!

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:25.090
Saint, can't you lend us some?

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:27.390
I did say I would offer assistance,

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:29.850
but I never agreed to spoil you.

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:32.500
I-In other words, we've been 
spending too much, huh?

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.110
Let's see... His target is

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:38.280
a pendant called Nosferatu's Saber.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.680
"The one who successfully captures 
this target will receive...

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:45.010
a reward of ten million"?! Damn!

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.550
And that's dead or alive, too!

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:51.990
Given that amount, there will obviously be 
a lot of people clamoring for the reward,

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.780
but it should still be 
a piece of cake for us.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.260
Time to show us the results 
of your training.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:09:59.340
Okay. I'll do my best.

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:01.120
I'll go with you.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.080
That's unusual...

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:07.280
You don't do things with us very often.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.590
You can't buy ammo if you don't have money.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.670
That's all there is to it.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.020
It's settled, then.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:22.680
Sold to No. 3, for five million.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.840
Damn... Five million?

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:33.040
Next, we have today's main attraction.

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:38.910
It's said that the king of vampires himself,
 Delacroix I, wore this pendant:

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:41.380
Nosferatu's Saber.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.370
Something's bothering you, isn't it?

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:48.950
For you to take action means this 
involves either Twilight or—

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.960
Foolish humans!

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.200
Keep your filthy hands off that pendant!

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:03.090
I'll be taking back my family's treasure!

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:04.900
A child?

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:12.140
I am he who carries on the name of 
Delacroix, head of the Nosferatu family,

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.510
the vampire, Delacroix II!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:29.490
I am he who carries on the name of 
Delacroix, head of the Nosferatu family,

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:32.530
the vampire, Delacroix II!

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:34.030
A vampire?

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:39.540
My family will never forgive humans.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.040
I will have revenge at any cost!

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:49.640
Revenge?

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.040
The Vampire War...

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:56.260
Two years ago, the British government 
started a large-scale operation

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:58.430
with the goal of eradicating all vampires.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:02.680
It was a war in name only. 
Really, it was a vampire hunt.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:06.640
It's what you'd call the dark 
history of the British Empire.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.280
Monster!

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.320
Run! He's a monster!

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.480
Eradicate...

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.410
Because they're... monsters?

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.710
A vampire, eh?

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:26.290
Please! You're just a kid!

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:30.310
Come quietly with us if you 
don't wanna get hurt.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:37.650
Those moves...

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.750
He's actually a real vampire?!

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.200
Fire! Fire!

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:49.870
Yes!

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:58.000
Beat it. He's my prey.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.500
You're...

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:06.000
It's been a long time,

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.250
Dracula.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.220
How dare you...

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.500
How dare you show yourself before me?

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.390
You are the one man I cannot forgive!

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:19.020
I haven't forgotten the
 day I let you escape.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:20.770
Van!

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:23.970
Van Helsing!

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.020
Let us settle our score.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:31.030
I'll be waiting at the place 
where you killed my father.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.040
If you want to kill me, then be there!

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:40.400
Hey, Van, was that...

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.860
Hey... Van!

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.160
Well, that turned into a big scene.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:51.420
So the "phantom thief under 
the moon" is a vampire...

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:54.240
And a survivor of vampire royalty, no less.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:57.200
It looks like you saw this coming.

00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:58.790
Sort of.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.280
Van was involved in the Vampire War?

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:05.450
At the time, Van had a very 
important duty to carry out

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.750
as a member of Twilight.

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:10.780
England's victory in the Vampire War

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.370
is said to have been attributed to him.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.590
An important duty?

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:20.080
To kill Delacroix, king of the vampires,
 and his entire family.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.170
That child may have survived somehow,

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:29.080
but after losing his family, 
he must have lived all this time alone.

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:31.080
Alone...

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:37.860
Van may have gone to pay his debt.

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:41.690
I won't sleep well if someone dies tonight.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:43.710
Let's go after Van.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.000
Please reconsider this plan!

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.370
They were a gentle race.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:12.120
The attack on humanity must 
have been a mistake!

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.320
I couldn't care less if it was.

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:20.140
As long as the British Empire can show off 
its military might to other countries,

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:22.390
who cares who dies?

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.030
You don't mean...

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:29.650
The attack by vampires was 
fabricated by the government?

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:34.320
What if it was? It doesn't 
change what your job is.

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:36.160
I can't do it!

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:40.650
Even if I hold your family's 
lives in my hand?

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:57.180
Father?

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:13.590
<i>I have to end it.</i>

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.920
I've been waiting for you, Helsing.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:32.860
Take that sword.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:36.590
Here, where my father died,

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:39.090
I will have your head!

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:46.710
My father's regret, my mother's grief,

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.600
and the anger of my compatriots...

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:51.190
I will avenge them all, here and now!

00:16:57.940 --> 00:16:59.430
This brings back memories.

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:02.290
Why did you betray him?! He trusted you!

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:05.150
Do you despise me, Dracula?

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.890
Don't call me that!

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:08.780
I inherited my father's name

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:11.030
on the day you killed him!

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.540
Of course I despise you!

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:22.330
Then fight me in earnest, Delacroix II.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:32.730
Wow, this place is really trashed.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:43.490
You said you'd take revenge on humanity...

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:45.500
And this is all you can do?

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:46.990
Shut up!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:57.040
You are weak.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:59.450
You can't even beat me.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:02.670
Don't underestimate me!

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:07.470
I've lived my whole life for the sake of 
killing you... killing all of humanity!

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:19.740
Lupin...

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.080
It's okay.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:26.740
You can't do that.

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:31.000
Give up on taking revenge on all humans.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:33.560
Give up, you say?

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.090
Then...

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:40.250
Where am I to direct my hatred?

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:42.870
It was you humans...

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.150
It was <i>you</i> who killed him!

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:51.210
I fulfilled my duty...

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:53.480
And yet... this...

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.470
Finis...

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.780
I'll give you my life.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:09.850
What?

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:12.660
There's something I must do.

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:15.540
I can't be killed just yet.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:20.310
But when it's all over, you can kill me.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:22.280
You have my word.

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:24.970
All the people here are my witnesses.

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:27.850
What are you planning by doing this?!

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:31.660
I won't accept that! 
Your atonement means nothing to me!

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:33.220
You don't have to accept it.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:38.580
So just put an end to your 
revenge by killing me.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:43.040
And don't hate anyone else anymore.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:08.590
Do you think...

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:13.590
we could take this boy back to our mansion?

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:18.610
I know he'll be lonely if we 
leave him in a place like this.

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:25.610
And there's no one in this world 
who has to live in isolation.

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.970
Come with us.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:32.910
Don't be ridiculous!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:36.440
I'm his grave keeper.
 I can't leave this place.

00:20:36.740 --> 00:20:38.400
Keep an eye on me.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.910
Then, one day, you can kill me

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:46.380
and offer me to your family, 
knowing you avenged them.

00:20:51.820 --> 00:20:53.770
Do you think he'll come?

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:58.610
You said you wanted to learn 
martial arts, didn't you?

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:00.640
I'm willing to teach you.

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:01.930
Huh?

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:04.160
I show no mercy, even to women.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:05.930
Are you prepared for that?

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:10.560
That's fine. Thank you, Van.

00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:18.060
<i>The sad color hasn't 
disappeared from your eyes.</i>

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:23.160
<i>but now, I think I can see the 
kindness hiding behind it.</i>

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:28.320
<i>Just like his hand welcomed me,</i>

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:33.210
<i>I'm sure there must be 
something I can do...</i>

00:23:11.780 --> 00:23:16.340
It's good you're training Cardia, 
but don't be too mean to her.

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:23.550
What you said then was not a lie, correct,

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:25.750
Helsing?

00:23:29.210 --> 00:23:31.560
Looks like we're having 
a welcome party today.

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:33.480
You'd better join in!

00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:38.460
Sure.
